  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.5203) clearly outperforms pca_n2000 (0.4849) as an RNA encoder in singleprofile rna_only settings, and image-only is very weak (0.2079). The major unexplored axis is whether multiprofile aggregation can further improve on the best singleprofile result. This experiment tests scvi_n200 with multiprofile + avgpool, isolating the effect of profile aggregation while holding the best-known encoder constant. Choosing avgpool over transformer keeps the comparison clean and avoids compounding two new variables (multiprofile + complex aggregation). If multiprofile+avgpool lifts accuracy above 0.52, it opens a promising direction for the remaining 6 experiments; if not, it confirms singleprofile is sufficient and we can pivot to testing scgpt or multimodal fusion with the best encoder. This is the highest-information experiment for reducing uncertainty about a core design axis with 6 experiments still remaining."
}

